<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia 1996 Jan-Sept palm oil exports rise.</title>
<headline>Indonesia 1996 Jan-Sept palm oil exports rise.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's palm oil exports rose 26.7 percent to $615.2 million in the first nine months of 1996 from $485.6 million and $436.5 million in the same period in 1995 and 1994, the government said on Monday.</p>
<p>The finance ministry released the data ahead of President Suharto's unveiling of the 1997/98 (April-March) state budget in parliament.</p>
<p>Indonesia is the world's largest producer of crude palm oil after neighbouring Malaysia.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom + 6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
